This refactor was supposed to keep behaviour the same, but the branch condition changed meaning:

::diff{file="packages/features/auth/lib/onboardingUtils.ts" lines="64-73"}

Before: invited users on v3 → personal settings; other v3 users → `/onboarding/getting-started`; non-v3 users → `/getting-started`.

After:
- **Every** v3 user who hasn't finished onboarding is sent to `/onboarding/personal/settings`. The `onboardingV3Enabled ? "/onboarding/getting-started"` branch on the last line can now never run, and new non-invited users never see plan selection.
- Users with a pending invite on legacy onboarding (v3 off) are sent to `/onboarding/personal/settings`, which is a v3 route, instead of `/getting-started`.

The PR description doesn't mention either change, and they don't follow from the goal.

